  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UD Peer Learning Event</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The assignment aims to organise a peer learning event under the Partner for Water (PVW) Bangladesh programme to facilitate knowledge sharing and evaluate the readiness of up to ten candidate pourashavas for the second cycle of the Urban Demonstrators (UD) initiative in Bangladesh.Building on the success of pilots conducted in the first cycle, the event will bring together representatives from pilot and candidate pourashavas to discuss lessons learned, potential interventions, and strategies for scaling the UD initiative.This assignment, supported by preliminary interviews, will assess land availability, governance quality, and local capacity to implement sustainable water infrastructure. The outcome will inform a go/no-go decision for PVW financing of the UD&apos;s second cycle and guide future upscaling efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
